%% the_meet · 02 · Bots
%% Source of truth: generate.py (CONFIG["bots"])
%% Three lifelines: the bot is the client, so there is no separate BOT actor.
%% AI-DESK only builds the query and hands it back; the client executes it on
%% DATAHUB directly, so execution never goes back through AI-DESK or the model.
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as CLIENT<br/>the configured bot<br/>Structured — from tables · Unstructured — from documents
    participant A as AI-DESK
    participant H as DATAHUB

    C->>A: the question, in plain English
    A->>A: 1 understands the question in plain English
    A->>A: 2 knows which data this bot may touch
    A->>A: 3 builds the query from the bot's own context
    A-->>C: the query
    C->>H: executes it directly on DATAHUB — not through AI-DESK
    H-->>C: the rows, from the attached source
    C->>C: the bot owns the answer — the model never executes
